A||||7||FieroGT||Carlisle in May, 2000, anyone?||||
Z||000000||FieroGT||09-08-1999||03:29 PM||||I was wondering if there would be any interest by any of the board members in attending the May show in Carlisle PA in May of next year. There are always a lot of Fieros, parts, and vendors. Overall, makes for a good outing. If there is any interest in this, I would like to hear about it.||||reg||
Z||000001||Silver Bullet||09-08-1999||01:20 PM||||I am very interested in the show.  Please keep details posted.  Thanks||||reg||
Z||000002||Phil||09-08-1999||07:26 PM||||I'm taking my 88 Formula to Carlisle as part of the Hot Rod Mag Power Tour||||reg||
Z||000003||FieroGT||09-08-1999||11:36 PM||||Phil:<P>When are you going? I'll be taking the Turbo Grand Prix with me to Carlisle on Saturday, October 2 for Fall Carlisle. I'm not showing the car or anything, just a few TGP owners getting together to hunt thru the vendors. I heard that there are factory service manuals that go for as little as $30! If that's the case, maybe I'll stock up on some Fiero stuff, as well. <P>All:<P>The reason I keep asking about a get-together is because I found out that it can be a lot of fun. The first time I got together with a few TGP owners, it was like a bunch of kids in the playground. Everyone had different backgrounds, and we sat talking, visited a junkyard, and combed used carlots together for an entire day, until the wives & girlfriends started calling to find out when the boys were getting back. It was a lot of fun, and I figured it would be great for anyone able to attend to do so. Keep it in mind; and I will be posting more about it as the time approaches. Save up your pennies now, there's only 9 months 'til the show!<P>||||reg||
Z||000004||SloPonti||09-09-1999||12:34 AM||||you guys should come to the carlise show in bloomington illinois!!!  i have been ever time sinced they first started in my area and no fiero parts and no fiero vendors show up!  come to us-we love fieros here!!!!||||reg||
Z||000005||theogre||09-09-1999||03:21 PM||||The Fiero portion of the show at Carlisle is actually sponsored/hosted/organized by the Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Assoc. (MAFOA)<P>They are the people who bring in not only the cars, but the vendors. The promotors of the rest of the show have little to nothing to do with it. I think part of the reason they even agree to do it is that many kit/replica packages are based on Fiero.<P>(Want to have some fun.... grab a DuPont registry and see how many Fieros you can find. there are nearly always a few.)||||reg||
Z||000006||Phil||09-09-1999||07:58 PM||||The Hot Rod Power Tour arrives in Carlisle Sunday October 10 about 4:00 pm. Monday morning they leave for Maryland. I'm only doing the Mass. to Carlisle portion.||||reg||
Z||000007||Taijiguy||09-10-1999||07:22 AM||||I'd suggest anyone planning on attending the Carlisle show, make your hotel reservations NOW...my dad goes every year, and makes his reservations for the following year as he checks out of the hotel. It's a madhouse, but it's a blast.||||reg||
